# Cloudflare Pages headers file. Read at edge time to set response
# headers for matching paths.
#
# Why we need this: Next.js 16 emits per-post Open Graph images at
# `/blog/<slug>/opengraph-image` (no file extension), and Cloudflare
# Pages defaults to `application/octet-stream` when the extension is
# missing. Most social crawlers content-sniff PNG bytes, but a few
# (LinkedIn, some bots) honor only `Content-Type` — so we set it
# explicitly to keep the share preview reliable everywhere.

/blog/*/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=604800
